            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 16 patches. The behavioral change adds a SessionStart entry to the projection hook family in engine/settings/projection.go and extends removeHooks in engine/settings/merge.go to scan SessionStart, so uninstall removes the new entry.",
              "Uninstall removal still uses the owned-entry identity check (ownedByAFamily). Foreign SessionStart entries are therefore not removed. projection_test.go checks this: a foreign SessionStart entry survives uninstall.",
              "The hook command is the Labdrian binary with the fixed event argument SessionStart. The patch shows no user-controlled input reaching a shell, no secrets, and no new dependencies.",
              "The status label changes and golden updates are consistent with each other. The new 'SessionStart projection hook' missing part appears in the drifted-state goldens.",
              "Test-only helper changes in golden_unix_test.go edit recorded text. They have no production reach."
            ]
          }
